<%--
_Sys_Form_Field - presentation around ONE panel input: label, required mark, help.

$label - the label, plain text [optional]
$required - shows an asterisk. PRESENTATION ONLY: it announces a SERVER rule and
            enforces nothing - validation lives in the endpoint, once.
$help - a muted line under the input, plain text [optional]

The input is the loose content, and $name goes on the INPUT, never here. Error
markup is not rendered here either: a failed submit is drawn by the form's one
error renderer, under the field it targets (this element is its .form-group).

    <_Sys_Form_Field $label="Explanation" $required=true $help="Recorded on the task.">
        <_Sys_Textarea_Input $name="explanation" $max_length=-1 />
    </_Sys_Form_Field>
--%>
<Define:_Sys_Form_Field tag="div" class="form-group">
    <% if (this.args.label) { %>
        <label class="_Sys_Form_Field__label form-label" $sid="label">
            <%= this.args.label %>
            <% if (this.args.required) { %>
                <span class="_Sys_Form_Field__required">*</span>
            <% } %>
        </label>
    <% } %>
    <div class="_Sys_Form_Field__control">
        <%= content() %>
    </div>
    <% if (this.args.help) { %>
        <div class="_Sys_Form_Field__help"><%= this.args.help %></div>
    <% } %>
</Define:_Sys_Form_Field>
